52b-58a5-8e5a-622fd4d5ea6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-64701" :question/problem "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}-15y=0$ where $y=y(t).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}-15{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -15) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -15 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -5)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64701/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4bcb5277-6d80-5cea-9688-ddb98f434093"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64701"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90705/selection/16468c0d799b267355052957889248c776fbcba0b77d703b25c8cd94d47f6dfb" :answer/id #uuid "9d53833c-5d1a-5b1a-83fb-a839e44aaeed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-4$ or $6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90705/selection/c731379b58ba9754bde6f7a9e3a5ba73396c45230c8f41a6b6723b8087638283" :answer/id #uuid "5fa724e5-7d2a-57e6-aa94-ecdc5e5ca610" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-6$ or $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90705/selection/cc73404f233abb2f330193eb3239bad39e0257268fbd8dc8bcc4bc17bc8c68ae" :answer/id #uuid "dbff2b53-56c5-52d4-84d3-c10292159c49" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-8$ or $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90705/selection/eb180b7816f4699339577dbe9862cd7fd02ab