6d5024ad4abd10bf62526606cd3a3151ae5b142fbcf94d9ee861d0f42d9021"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-90720" :question/id #uuid "21d26124-87b6-59dc-b996-f57deec2c2f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-90720" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-7\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+6y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-7\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+6{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +6) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +6=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -6)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =1$ or $\\lambda =6.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{6x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-90720/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe7e5c4f-6ac0-58e8-8b95-fe5a2230341c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90720"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130114/selection/b70ab47bb0e62b24fc4dd3733dd82e5c284b591b714035370d6ac53ca7aba030" :answer/id #uuid "c5558a64-a793-5309-9748-ca339be72344" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130114/selection/f2f6ab1bae5e0155ffdabdd7541837efeda32881eb6e4c9df5e48c4e2e3fedf4" :answer/id #uuid "cc1498fd-9670-5c71-b89c-0afee33afc14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130114/selection/5e6cd28f8424f1