d differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+3{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =-1.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-3x}$ and ${e}^{-x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${e}^{3x}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130123/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcb5d818-acb0-53c7-90f9-328256600175"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130123"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-90725/selection/ed95ced6815ff74862391786b341c83742b2a88d3c9a0053a9376da5eba65b1c" :answer/id #uuid "ccf71fbd-65e7-5ff0-bb84-f036fd3a58cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{-5x}+3{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90725/selection/32f1766c0c6421ef2dd76fdfd9a0cc2cef4aa1b65b4e62182380e16d6dd580cb" :answer/id #uuid "0f7bf6d9-7205-5cdc-81b4-681552c14e60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90725/selection/5d7f37be3535ec9c67d6383d49deee24e3bd64d55c1c1c0c02a25695e9e7b1eb" :answer/id #uuid "d37846a4-71bd-53c2-90d5-8137e9611293" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-90725/selection/2d0460c52a16c5e5f9762777c06881e68f0918a14c3028ee494ece894e2252c8" :answer/id #uuid "2b918f7b-e6