a +5)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =-5.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-3x}$ and ${e}^{-5x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${e}^{5x}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-90725/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fcb5d818-acb0-53c7-90f9-328256600175"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-90725"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130124/selection/812f71be3f1d547f965f196d93bcc823e6c9fc09155dda81483276f5e788fd31" :answer/id #uuid "859db23e-9b05-5df1-9b15-a83e530ad24b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{e}^{-3x}+4{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130124/selection/5d7f37be3535ec9c67d6383d49deee24e3bd64d55c1c1c0c02a25695e9e7b1eb" :answer/id #uuid "87ec3935-ebf1-5e5e-aa14-4fade6f9ecfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130124/selection/33cdcb26c61f9871ea89373d3d976b3055aa7f285d3cfb44def3a3662dcb91f0" :answer/id #uuid "89f2c543-1b79-5e92-98b9-108a3cdd34bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}+{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130124/selection/feee356f06ee10e634d913a8f8d7f1c87fc0041c763ae01b1c0b6d9e39e8e7a5" :answer/id #uuid "4f1bc561-0b11-5903-88c2-eb0998653a50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130124/selection/da580dd1fb412f89f99ee97b8962a88d9e17ea278d2288047977f003972a99ca" :answer/id #uuid "337326d2-c866-57f6-80c8-46cda2cab705" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}+{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130124/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4dad484e-42b3-5fc2-a470-4b352c2c5f6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-13012